From 7dbeb6935ac331b0cba6c41cabd8e9d02d5f64ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chandrashekar Devegowda <chandrashekar.devegowda@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:10:21 +0530
Subject: Bluetooth: btintel_pcie: fix plen overflow in btintel_pcie_recv_frame()
Git-commit: 7dbeb6935ac331b0cba6c41cabd8e9d02d5f64ea
Patch-mainline: v7.3-rc6
References: git-fixes CVE-2026-98731 bsc#1286674

plen is u16 and computed as HDR_SIZE + dlen. For ACL/ISO frames dlen
is a 16-bit field, so a value >= 0xFFFC wraps the sum, bypassing the
"skb->len < plen" check and letting skb_trim() truncate the packet.

Widen plen to u32 so the addition cannot wrap.

Fixes: c2b636b3f788 ("Bluetooth: btintel_pcie: Add support for PCIe transport")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Chandrashekar Devegowda <chandrashekar.devegowda@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.von.dentz@intel.com>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 drivers/bluetooth/btintel_pcie.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btintel_pcie.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btintel_pcie.c
index 2819e001797b..d05af27790f9 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btintel_pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btintel_pcie.c
@@ -1197,7 +1197,7 @@ static int btintel_pcie_recv_frame(struct btintel_pcie_data *data,
 {
 	int ret;
 	u8 pkt_type;
-	u16 plen;
+	u32 plen;
 	u32 pcie_pkt_type;
 	void *pdata;
 	struct hci_dev *hdev = data->hdev;
-- 
2.55.0

